remediation:
Implement strict HTTP method validation on the change_password.php endpoint. Only allow POST method and reject all other methods with HTTP 405 Method Not Allowed response. Add the following code at the beginning of the file:

```php
if ($_SERVER['REQUEST_METHOD'] !== 'POST') {
    http_response_code(405);
    header('Allow: POST');
    exit(json_encode(['success' => false, 'message' => 'Method not allowed']));
}
```

Additionally, ensure that the session cookie is configured with proper security flags (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite) to prevent CSRF attacks even if this method validation is bypassed.
